WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:06.100
NBC's proposed Xena reboot may have been scrapped
by the studio in 2017, but that doesn't mean

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.180
fans of the warrior princess can't still get
their hit.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:14.620
After all, iconic Xena actor Lucy Lawless
is still out there, and she's been very busy indeed.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.800
Here's all the great stuff that's happened
for the Xena star since the end of her breakout

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:19.800
'90s role.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:24.720
Having forged her career as one of the greatest
cult icons of our time, Lawless has since

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.400
managed to maintain that status by appearing
in dozens of beloved shows.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:33.820
In 2006, she starred as an FBI agent attempting
to extract some sensitive information from

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:38.800
Neptune's savviest teenage detective in Veronica
Mars, and a year later she enjoyed a guest

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.650
appearance on Curb Your Enthusiasm as a version
of herself stuck on an excruciatingly bad

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:45.100
date with Larry David.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:49.520
Lawless has also enjoyed a number of other
unexpected guest appearances, which have included

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:54.329
comedies such as Flight of the Conchords,
dramas like Top of the Lake and Burn Notice,

00:00:54.329 --> 00:00:56.920
and comic book adaptations like Agents of
S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.220
"Hello, I'm Murray."

00:00:58.380 --> 00:00:59.440
"Hello there Murray."

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:00.600
"Stop shaking her hand."

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:06.400
For years, many diehard fans of Xena have
maintained that the rumored romance between

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:11.260
Xena and Gabrielle amounted to far more than
just innuendo and queer subtext.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:15.820
And in 2003, Lawless was happy to confirm
that the two were definitely gay.

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:16.680
The actor said:

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:21.360
"It wasn't just that Xena was bisexual and
kinda like her gal pal and they kind of fooled

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:24.140
around sometimes, it was 'Nope, they're married,
man.'"

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:29.280
As well as enjoying an appearance on the groundbreaking
LGBT drama The L Word, Lawless has attended

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:34.280
various celebrations and events in proud public
support of the LGBT community.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:40.579
In 2017, she even received the Ally of the
Year Award at the 2017 Australian LGBTI Awards

00:01:40.579 --> 00:01:46.860
and in 2018 attended the inaugural New Zealand
LGBTI Awards Ceremony as their proud ambassador.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:50.700
While speaking about the influence Xena had
in providing visibility and encouragement

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:55.160
to the lesbian community, Lawless describes
Xena fans as being "a force for good" that

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:56.720
she's "immensely grateful for."

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:57.440
Lawless said:

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:02.060
"Nobody else outside of our world is going
to understand or appreciate that but I know,

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:04.780
and they know that that was a profound experience
for all of us."

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:10.399
Anyone with a fond memory of the groundbreaking
musical episodes of Xena will already be aware

00:02:10.399 --> 00:02:12.210
that Lawless is kind of an amazing singer.

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:16.600
What you may not be aware of, however, is
just how much Lawless loves being a musician.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:22.580
In 2009, the actor was a contestant on the
Australian singing competition Celebrity Duets,

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:27.160
where she sang opposite such musical legends
as Dionne Warwick and Bonnie Tyler.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:31.239
Having had a background in musical theater,
Lawless has returned to her roots by leading

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:33.380
a show called Pleasuredome: The Musical.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:38.280
Billed as a "dirty urban musical" with a queer
love story at its core, the camp '80s-set

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:43.260
musical is produced by her husband and focuses
on a female business owner, played by Lawless,

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.480
standing up against a bigoted businessman.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:49.660
Lawless told the New Zealand Herald that the
musical feels more timely than ever today,

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:51.719
since the LGBT community is:

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:54.260
"...under threat like it hasn't been since
the '70s."

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:58.819
In her opinion, however, the visibility that
shows such as Pleasuredome gives the LGBT

00:02:58.819 --> 00:03:00.209
community is the answer.

00:03:00.209 --> 00:03:01.209
She said:

00:03:01.209 --> 00:03:05.689
"People that love and support and accept [the
LGBT community] need to band together and

00:03:05.689 --> 00:03:08.189
show that there are more of us than there
are of the detractors.

00:03:08.189 --> 00:03:10.520
We have to win this for the sake of everybody."

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:15.680
Fans of the quirky cult filmmaker Sam Raimi
will likely know that he prefers to work with

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:17.319
the same people time and again.

00:03:17.319 --> 00:03:20.829
And while he might not have as much of a screen
presence in Raimi's productions as actors

00:03:20.829 --> 00:03:25.239
like Bruce Campbell, Robert Tapert shares
a number of producer credits with Raimi.

00:03:25.239 --> 00:03:29.980
The two have worked together on projects including
The Grudge, Don't Breathe, The Evil Dead franchise,

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:32.170
and, of course, Xena: Warrior Princess.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:37.340
Tapert and Lawless obviously made a terrific
impression on one another, because in 1998,

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:39.819
the star of Xena went on to marry the producer.

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:43.459
They remain married to this day, and still
work as creative collaborators.

00:03:43.459 --> 00:03:48.730
In 2011, Lawless appeared in Raimi and Tapert's
Spartacus series before snagging a supporting

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:54.120
role in Ash vs Evil Dead in 2015, even though
the actor confessed to being less than a fan

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.440
of the original movie when it was first released.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:04:00.239
Lawless made the surprising confession in
an interview with Rotten Tomatoes, where she

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:04.999
admitted that she was so outraged by The Evil
D ead as a 17-year-old that she marched out

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:07.400
of the movie after the infamous tree scene.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:08.200
She said:

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:12.180
"I was so mortally offended that I got up
and I stomped out saying, 'These people are

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.860
misogynists and sick and that movie's awful.'

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:17.510
Twelve years later, I was married to one of
them.

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:18.500
Trick of fate."

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:23.600
Though Lawless has enjoyed a diverse career
since leaving Xena, it's also easy to imagine

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:28.160
that the actor may have been typecast in a
very specific type of role: a strong, ferocious

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.580
woman who typically shows up in period pieces.

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:35.170
And the actor has indeed returned to such
roles time and again in productions like Salem

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:36.340
and Spartacus.

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:40.280
And although she's clearly proud of these
roles, according to a conversation with Interview

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:44.180
Magazine, these "tough woman" characters aren't
the ones that interest her the most.

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:48.500
Crucially, Lawless is interested in seeking
out characters who allow her to reflect on

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:52.890
her own life and identity, and from the sounds
of it, much of that has little to do with

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:54.240
being a warrior princess.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:55.720
Lawless told Interview Magazine:

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:59.040
"As an artist, you want to be able to explore
facets of yourself.

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:02.960
The roles that I'm proudest of…are the ones
where I get to be a stain on the wall…I

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:07.200
like to play women who are not strong at all,
because there's certainly plenty of myself

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.520
that is no kind of a warrior."

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:12.740
Possessing the nerd-cred that she does, it
made sense when Lawless joined the cast of

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:15.560
the Battlestar Galactica reboot in 2005.

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:20.760
Arriving in the eighth episode of Season 2,
Lawless depicts D'Anna Biers, a trashy tabloid

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:25.400
reporter for the Fleet News Service who is
filming a warts-and-all report about the Galactica.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:29.800
The episode is disarmingly fun and lighthearted,
but it comes with a bombshell at the end that

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:34.410
has been called one of Lawless' most unexpected
TV scenes ever: the revelation that Biers

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:35.240
is a Cylon.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:36.440
"Yeah.

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:40.960
It truly is a miracle from God."

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:45.460
Considering Lawless' apparent love for philosophy,
it's perhaps unsurprising that the religious

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:50.480
aspect of some of the deeper themes of Battlestar
Galactica are what drew the actor to the show.

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:55.380
Lawless told Galactica.tv that she saw D'Anna
as a character consumed by the nature of the

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:59.620
philosophy of God, and she loved the character's
complex, questioning spirit.

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:00.620
Lawless explained:

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:05.020
"She was a zealot, she was an outlaw, she
was a betrayer and yet she saw herself as

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:06.580
a great patriot in a way."

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:11.440
By far one of Lawless' most beloved roles
since leaving Xena has to be that of Diane

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:16.320
Lewis on Parks and Recreation, the single
mother with whom Nick Offerman's Ron Swanson

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:18.710
falls madly in love, and eventually marries.

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:22.840
A self-confessed Parks &amp; Rec superfan, the
role was a huge win for Lawless.

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:28.120
Lawless only appeared in ten episodes of the
widely adored comedy between 2012 and 2014,

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:31.980
but her character was pivotal in taking Swanson
out of his comfort zone.

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:40.400
Diane transformed Ron from a surly bachelor
into a surly husband and father, giving the

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:45.160
character something he had never had before
on the show: a genuinely healthy romantic relationship.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:49.600
Lawless has also confessed that Diane is the
character closest to her own personality of

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:51.200
anyone she's ever played.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:55.380
On top of that, she has also admitted to being
something of an aficionado for the show, who

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:59.280
had seen every episode prior to stepping foot
on set, to the point that she was able to

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:02.740
correct Offerman about Parks and Rec continuity
during filming.

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:07.560
A self-described "court ghoul," Lawless is
something of a true-crime fanatic who is so

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:12.400
fascinated with the subject that she even
attends real-life trials whenever she has the chance.

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:14.260
As she told the Associated Press:

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:18.890
"It just teaches you so much about life and
your own society and justice and about yourself.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:21.820
It’s really important that we participate
in the democracy.

00:07:21.820 --> 00:07:25.880
That’s a really good way to hold the justice
system to the standards of the people."

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:29.500
She has also discussed the thrill of chatting
about trials with the cops and journalists

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:30.500
involved afterwards.

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:34.670
And that fascination appears to have led her
to one of her more recent projects, the Acorn

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:39.960
TV streaming series My Life Is Murder, which
she says "closely mirrors" her personal interests.

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:44.680
And it's probably no surprise that the character
so closely aligns with many of Lawless' interests,

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:48.920
since the star has stated that creator Claire
Tonkin wrote the role with her in mind.

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:50.160
Lawless told AP News:

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:53.560
"There's a lot of me in the character and
that's the advantage of having writers build

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:54.770
something around you.

00:07:54.770 --> 00:07:55.940
I'm a very lucky woman."

00:07:56.860 --> 00:08:01.120
Beyond her acting career, Lawless has also
demonstrated a firm commitment to fighting

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:02.250
for the environment.

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:07.090
The Xena star is a passionate activist and
even worked with Greenpeace as a climate ambassador

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:08.090
in 2012.

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:12.580
Clearly, the title wasn't just for show, as
the star joined in on some direct action and

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:16.780
was arrested along with seven other activists
after climbing to the top of a Shell oil drilling

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:20.260
ship in opposition of planned oil drilling
operations in the Arctic.

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:24.340
At the time, Lawless stated that her reasons
for the protest were logical, saying:

00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:28.460
"I believe passionately that renewable energy
is the way of the future…We don't have to

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:31.490
go to the ends of the earth to suck out every
last drop of oil.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:35.860
Instead we need to smarten up and begin the
transition to a clean, green, sustainable

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:39.810
energy future and right now that means keeping
Shell out of the Arctic."

00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:43.620
During interviews that followed her arrest,
Lawless remained proud of her actions and

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:48.060
insisted that her celebrity, something she
calls "a very silly kind of currency", helped

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:52.200
to raise visibility and awareness in the urgent
fight against climate change.

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:56.640
Lawless later pleaded guilty to trespassing
charges and was ordered by a New Zealand judge

00:08:56.640 --> 00:09:00.800
to pay a minor fine and complete 120 hours
of community service.

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:05.300
In interviews, Lawless has stated that she
and her siblings were raised by their hardworking

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:07.320
parents to be what she calls "contributors."

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:08.650
She told Stuff:

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:12.610
"On the weekends, Mum and Dad would visit
people, maybe they were sick or celebrating

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:14.580
their diamond jubilee, that sort of thing."

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:19.490
Since leaving Xena, it's clear that contributing
to communities and to good causes has continued

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:20.990
to be a great passion of hers.

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:25.080
Over the past couple of decades, Lawless has
done a great deal of work for various charities

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:30.820
aiding LGBT people, environmental causes,
breast cancer research, and HIV/AIDS causes.

00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:35.150
She even sits on the board of trustees for
The Starship Foundation, which provides fundraising

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:37.660
efforts for New Zealand's largest children's
hospital.

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:41.960
And Lawless' altruistic nature has long inspired
her fans to do the same.

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:46.860
In 2007, Lawless and her fans set up Feel
the Love Week, an annual charity drive at

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:51.270
the end of September that encourages fans
to support a charity they care about, be it

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:53.880
by donating money, supplies, or volunteering.

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:58.480
Speaking to Vice in 2017, Lawless suggested
it's the thing she's most proud of in her

00:09:58.480 --> 00:09:59.560
career thus far.

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:00.300
She said:

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:04.060
"People started doing random acts of kindness
in their communities rather than giving to

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:05.870
my charity or something I'm involved in.

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:10.400
I asked them to go and do something to enrich
their own communities and we did amazing things."

